From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] wlserver: a touch does not show the cursor

With the default touch click mode (Left), a touch moves the pointer to
the finger and clicks there, and the warp revealed the cursor, so every
tap drew an arrow under the finger that stayed up for the 10 s cursor
timeout. Passthrough mode avoids it, but OpenGamepadUI (Godot on
Xwayland) does not act on the passed-through touches, so taps stopped
working there.

Keep the emulated click and drop the arrow. Touch-driven warps are
synthetic, so they don't reveal the cursor, and they hide one a real
mouse left visible. A mouse or trackpad moving again shows it as before.

(qforge: UX, MANGMI Air X / Air Y touchscreens, 2026-10-11.)
---
diff --git a/src/wlserver.cpp b/src/wlserver.cpp
index 0ceaa1e..df0c7c5 100644
--- a/src/wlserver.cpp
+++ b/src/wlserver.cpp
@@ -3121,6 +3121,19 @@ void wlserver_mousewarp( double x, double y, uint32_t time, bool bSynthetic )
 	wlr_seat_pointer_notify_frame( wlserver.wlr.seat );
 }
 
+// A touch emulating the mouse moves the pointer to the finger, but a finger needs no arrow under
+// it: warp without revealing the cursor, and hide one a real mouse left visible. A mouse or
+// trackpad moving again shows it as usual (wlserver_mousemotion/mousewarp).
+void wlserver_touch_mousewarp( double x, double y, uint32_t time )
+{
+	wlserver_mousewarp( x, y, time, true );
+	if ( !wlserver.bCursorHidden )
+	{
+		wlserver.bCursorHidden = true;
+		wlserver_oncursorevent();
+	}
+}
+
 void wlserver_fake_mouse_pos( double x, double y )
 {
 	// Fake a pos for eg. hiding true cursor state from Steam.
@@ -3292,7 +3305,7 @@ void wlserver_touchmotion( double x, double y, int touch_id, uint32_t time, bool
 		{
 			g_bPendingTouchMovement = true;
 
-			wlserver_mousewarp( tx, ty, time, false );
+			wlserver_touch_mousewarp( tx, ty, time );
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -3340,7 +3353,7 @@ void wlserver_touchdown( double x, double y, int touch_id, uint32_t time, gamesc
 
 			if ( eMode != gamescope::TouchClickModes::Trackpad )
 			{
-				wlserver_mousewarp( tx, ty, time, false );
+				wlserver_touch_mousewarp( tx, ty, time );
 			}
 
 			uint32_t button = TouchClickModeToLinuxButton( eMode );
